 "topic": "Angles, triangles and quadrilaterals",
 "holiday_lesson": 8,
 "goal": "I can use angle facts to find unknown angles step by step, and give a reason for every step.",
 "learn": {
  "intro": "Crossing lines make equal opposite angles. Drawings are not to scale.",
  "example": {
   "problem": "In the figure, AB = AC and angle BAC = 48°. BCD is a straight line. Find angle ACD. Give a reason for each step.",
   "steps": [
    "AB = AC, so triangle ABC is isosceles. The angles at B and C are equal.",
    "The angles of a triangle add up to 180°. 180° - 48° = 132°.",
    "Angle ACB = 132° ÷ 2 = 66° (equal base angles).",
    "BCD is a straight line, so ACD = 180° - 66° = 114° (angles on a straight line)."
   ],
   "answer": "Angle ACD = 114°.",
